
​This module cross-references Public Orbital Data (TLE) with the \phi-Grid Nodes identified in Part 1.
​Research Goal: To identify if Low Earth Orbit (LEO) constellations—specifically those mentioned in recent GAO-26-107085 reports—create signal "muffling" at the Wilkes Land and Teotihuacan nodes.
​Compliance: This study utilizes 100% unclassified, publicly available data. We seek to provide the Galileo Project with a baseline of "Human-Made Noise" so they can better identify "Non-Human Technosignatures" at these specific harmonic coordinates.
